{{Top|notoc=1}}
{{Quote|That's no moon. It's a space station.|[[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], upon seeing the Death Star|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>|audio=ThatsNoMoon-ANH.flac}}
[[File:DS1DeathStar-TSWB.png|thumb|right|250px|The space station known as the Death Star]]
'''Space stations''' or simply '''stations''' were artificial<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref> structures in constructed to remain in [[Realspace|space]].<ref name="SW EOSAOV (SE)">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles (second edition)]]''</ref> Some, like the [[Citadel of Rur]]<ref name="Aphra 5">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 5|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 5]]</ref> and [[Faos Station]],<ref name="ItNofR">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref> were stationed independently in deep space or even in [[nebula]]s.<ref name="The Steal">''[[Adventures in Wild Space: The Steal]]''</ref> Many stations were capable of being in [[orbit]] of astronomical objects, such as the [[Sorca Retreat]].<ref name="Aphra 9">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 9|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 9]]</ref>

Stations commissioned for military use often had emplacements of defensive mechanisms consisting of technologies like [[turbolaser]] batteries. Some stations could mobilize and navigate through both realspace and [[hyperspace]].<ref name="Episode IV" />

The [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|DS-1 Death Star Mobile Battle Station]]<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> and the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station]]<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> were constructed by the command of [[Darth Sidious]], publicly known as the [[Supreme Chancellor]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] and later [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Catalyst" /> The two Death Stars were also classified as [[battle station]]s, a type of space station.<ref name="Episode IV" /><ref name="Episode VI" />

During or after [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Pals Date">{{GalacticPalsDate}}</ref> the [[Safari droid]] [[M1-RE]], a specialized member of the [[Galactic Society of Creature Enthusiasts]], was stationed on the [[Youngling Care Space Station]] where she cared for and studied several species of [[youngling]]s.<ref name="Learn to care">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-galactic-pals|text=Learn to Care for Creatures and Aliens in ''Star Wars Galactic Pals''}}</ref> The station was very large and had several rooms,<ref name="Wookiee">{{GalacticPals|Wookiee}}</ref> including one that was designed to resemble the [[Endor|Forest Moon of Endor]].<ref name="Ewok">{{GalacticPals|Ewok}}</ref>

